CTR UEFI licensing and third-party notices
=========================================

CTR UEFI's original source is available under the GNU General Public
License, version 2 or any later version (GPL-2.0-or-later). LICENSE
contains version 2. The source files and the notices below identify the
terms that apply to the incorporated third-party material.

Firmware distributions must include LICENSE, NOTICE, and the applicable
license texts from Licenses/. Provide the complete corresponding source
for each released binary under the GPL, including the source for the
matching project revision, the EDK II code and headers used from the
two revisions below, the local patches, and the scripts used to build,
link, and package the firmware. Run `make source-archive` from a Git
checkout with initialized submodules and clean build inputs to create
`build/ctr-uefi-source.tar.gz`. Run it from the same project working
tree used to build the release binary. The archive takes project files
from that working tree and upstream files from the commits recorded in
the Git index. It contains the EDK II packages used by the firmware,
the EDK II host build tools' source and configuration, and the pinned
FatPkg source. Extract it and run `./build.sh` with the host build
prerequisites, including `arm-none-eabi-gcc` 8 or later for
`-ffile-prefix-map`. The build script can download Python 2.7 if a
suitable interpreter is unavailable.

